Hi all,
I cannot succeed getting a decent wireless connection with a Samsung 305U1A
netbook.
Wireless card is a Broadcom 4313. The card has been just in-warranty
replaced but the issue still persists. Windows7 connection is stable, as it
was before card replacement.
OS is Slackware Linux 14. I tried stock kernel 3.2.29, then compiled 3.4.18,
and finally latest compat-wireless sources (3.6.6). The issue is always the
same: dmesg show timeouts and a driver crash.
Sometimes I can associate with AP and navigate, but after a while connection
drops and stays disconnected until reboot.
I attach logs and configuration (with compat-3.6.6 modules). Let me know if
I can help further.
